imed direction, signed -0.0061 with upper bound only +0.0159, below the outcome_004 clinical threshold, so it is rejected and closed. The outcome_012 transfer H38 is also very weak: +0.0037, CI -0.0183 to +0.0257. Its upper bound only barely reaches the standard clinical threshold, so I defer rather than accept, but it is low priority. The interaction tests H40 and H41 do not support the registered interaction directions and their upper bounds do not establish meaningful effect modification under my interpretive threshold, so they are rejected/closed; their wide intervals reflect limited precision and interaction coding is less directly interpretable than subgroup main effects. H44, the feature_052 transfer to outcome_012 within feature_002=1, is opposite the claimed direction and has upper bound +0.0187 below the outcome_012 threshold, so it is rejected. The broad screens H26, H28, and H30 are near null or opposite and have upper bounds below their respective clinical thresholds, so they are rejected/closed. H25, feature_034 on outcome_005, is not clinically compelling because the point estimate is only +0.0102, although its upper bound +0.0261 marginally crosses the 0.025 threshold; I therefore defer rather than reject. Overall, the only new candidate strong enough for validation is H39. If validation replicates a clinically meaningful positive estimate, it can be accepted as a separate dataset-specific association; if not, the feature_052 line for outcome_006 should be downgraded and attention can return to H16 and H37. No conclusions here imply causality, mechanism, or generalizability beyond the supplied dataset, and predictor labels are opaque."
