  "narrative": "All delivered estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 mean differences, a positive signed estimate corresponds to stronger dependency (more negative score) in exposed versus comparator; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate corresponds to weaker dependency (less negative/higher score). I used the approximate practical threshold based on mean absolute dependency magnitude, about 0.0093 for outcome_006 and outcome_014. All new Welch cells met the minimum n=20 requirement, and I did not detect obvious leakage or coding error; however these remain single-dataset discovery comparisons with heavy multiplicity and no remaining independent validation budget. H179 is the clearest new supported finding: within feature_002=1 and feature_060=1, feature_011=1 versus feature_011=0 is associated with stronger outcome_006 dependency, signed estimate +0.0926 with 95% interval +0.0114 to +0.1739. The lower bound is above the practical threshold, so I accept this as a dataset-specific associative finding, but it remains low-confidence for generalizability and could be a rare-subgroup/multiplicity artifact; I close it rather than continue validation because validation is unavailable. The feature_006/outcome_014 localization is inconclusive for broadening. H178 is positive but imprecise (interval -0.0999 to +0.2275), so the formal interaction within feature_002=1 is not established. H181 and H182 are positive in the feature_002=0 feature_060 strata but both cross null and have lower bounds well below threshold. Therefore I do not expand feature_006 beyond the already accepted global H155 and the narrow feature_002=1/feature_060=0 localization H168; the feature_002=0 cells are deferred as weak context-dependent screens. H183 is opposite to its registered direction and imprecise, so the registered interaction within feature_002=0 is not supported and is closed. The feature_007 reversed lead remains only low-confidence hypothesis-generating: H180, H184, and H185 have positive signed estimates but wide intervals with lower bounds below the practical threshold. Together with the global reversed signal H165, this is directionally suggestive for weaker dependency with feature_007=1, especially for outcome_006, but not robustly supported. I keep H180/H184/H185 active because I propose one more localization test for outcome_014 in feature_002=0. H175 and H186 test feature_029 across the two main outcomes; both are opposite to the registered stronger-dependency direction and not statistically convincing, so both are rejected and closed as weak screens. H188 is essentially null for feature_062/outcome_014 and is closed. H187 is the most important negative/opposite screen: the registered hypothesis was that feature_063 level_002 is associated with stronger dependency, but the signed estimate is -0.0361 with interval -0.0701 to -0.0022. That corresponds to a raw positive difference, i.e. weaker outcome_014 dependency for level_002 versus level_001. I reject the original direction and propose a reversed claim plus a companion outcome_006 test, although the reversed lower bound will still be near/below the practical threshold and requires independent confirmation that is not available. No validation was requested because remaining independent validation requests are zero.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported dataset-specific associative findings: (1) H15/H37 localize feature_060=1 to stronger outcome_006/outcome_014 dependency within feature_002=0, but validation intervals remain wide. (2) H155/H168 support feature_006=1 as stronger outcome_014 dependency globally and especially within feature_002=1/feature_060=0; this remains narrow because H178/H181/H182 did not establish a broader or formal feature_060 effect modification. (3) H179 supports feature_011=1 as stronger outcome_006 dependency specifically in feature_002=1/feature_060=1; this is accepted for this dataset but is rare-subgroup, single-outcome, unvalidated, and multiplicity-sensitive. Low-confidence leads: reversed feature_007 weaker dependency remains active but not accepted because H165 lower bound is below threshold and H172/H173/H180/H184/H185 are mostly imprecise positive point estimates. Feature_063 level_002 versus level_001 shows a statistically significant reverse association for outcome_014 in original direction -1; H187 is rejected, but a reversed claim is proposed along with outcome_006 companion, pending same-direction coherence and practical-threshold caution. Feature_029 and feature_062 are closed as weak negative/opposite screens. Next priorities: test feature_063 reversal/companion, test feature_011/outcome_014 in the accepted feature_002=1/feature_060=1 cell, and complete feature_007 localization for outcome_014 in feature_002=0. No independent validation budget remains, so all conclusions must remain dataset-specific, associative, and not causal or generalizable."
