  "narrative": "All 12 newly delivered estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. I audited them for leakage, coding errors, cell-size requirements, and competing explanations. The Welch cells all satisfy the minimum n=20 rule, and the comparisons appear correctly specified. However, none of the new discovery results provides a same-direction lower bound above the approximate practical threshold for the relevant outcome scale, so I accept no new claim. For outcome_006 and outcome_014, the practical threshold remains about 0.0093; for outcome_011, it is about 0.030, based on the approximate absolute dependency score scale.\n\nH190 is a companion test of the reversed feature_063 lead for outcome_006. The signed weaker-dependency estimate is +0.0218, but the interval is negative-to-positive (-0.0126 to +0.0563). This is statistically inconclusive and the lower bound is far below the practical threshold. Since H189 for outcome_014 already had a lower bound below practical relevance and the outcome_011 companion H197 is essentially null, I reject H190 and downgrade H189 to deferred rather than keep it as an active lead.\n\nH191 tests the feature_007 reversed weaker-dependency signal for outcome_014 within feature_002=0. The signed estimate is -0.0177, i.e., the raw contrast is in the opposite direction from the registered weaker-dependency hypothesis, and the interval crosses null. I reject H191 and close it. Combined with the imprecise or null feature_007 interaction tests H198 and H199, and the wide stratified mean-difference tests H172, H173, H180, H184, and H185, the feature_007 reversed-dependency lead is not scientifically meaningful across the examined strata. I close those stratified leads. H165 remains unresolved because it is statistically positive at the global outcome_006 level, but its lower bound (+0.0056) is below the practical threshold and could be a multiplicity-sensitive dataset-specific signal; I close the investigation because no independent validation is available.\n\nThe feature_011 localization for outcome_014 remains inconclusive. H192 is in the previously accepted feature_002=1/feature_060=1 cell for outcome_006, and H192 gives a positive signed stronger-dependency estimate of +0.0278 for outcome_014, but the interval is wide and crosses null (-0.0612 to +0.1168). H195 is positive in the feature_060=0 complement (+0.0633, interval -0.0270 to +0.1536), and H196 is negative for the feature_060=1 interaction (-0.0355, interval -0.1616 to +0.0905). This pattern does not support robust localization of feature_011 to feature_060=1 for outcome_014, but it also does not strongly refute a broader positive association. Therefore I leave H192 and H195 unresolved but deferred, while rejecting the formal interaction H196.\n\nThe feature_011 and feature_006 companion-outcome tests are negative. H193 tests feature_006 on outcome_006 in the accepted feature_002=1/feature_060=0 localization for outcome_014; the signed estimate is negative (-0.0228) and imprecise (-0.1496 to +0.1040), so it does not support transfer to outcome_006. H194 tests feature_011 on outcome_011 in the accepted feature_002=1/feature_060=1 cell for outcome_006; the signed estimate is negative (-0.0413) and imprecise (-0.1087 to +0.0260). Thus the accepted feature_011/outcome_006 finding appears outcome-specific in this dataset, not a broad dependency marker for outcome_011. I reject and close both.\n\nH197 tests feature_063 level_002 versus level_001 for outcome_011 in the reversed weaker-dependency direction; the estimate is tiny and null-like (+0.0028, interval -0.0218 to +0.0274), so it is rejected. H198 and H199 test feature_007 by feature_060 interactions within feature_002=1 for outcome_006 and outcome_014. H198 is negative and wide (-0.0189, interval -0.1725 to +0.1347), and H199 is positive but far below practical relevance (+0.0084, interval -0.1578 to +0.1745). Neither supports a localized weaker-dependency feature_007 effect, so both are rejected and closed.\n\nThe broad screens H31 (feature_021 for outcome_003) and H33 (feature_012 for outcome_011) are also null or opposite to the registered stronger-dependency direction and are rejected and closed.\n\nOverall, this batch weakens the secondary leads around feature_007, feature_063, feature_011 outcome_014 transfer, and feature_006 outcome_006 transfer. The currently accepted dataset-specific associative findings remain unchanged, but the evidence against unvalidated broad or companion effects has increased. No validation is requested because the independent validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "No new accepted findings from iteration 15. All new discovery evidence remains single-dataset, multiplicity-sensitive, and unvalidated. Current accepted associative set still consists of feature_006 associated with stronger outcome_014 dependency globally, feature_006 associated with stronger outcome_014 in feature_002=1/feature_060=0, and feature_011 associated with stronger outcome_006 in feature_002=1/feature_060=1. These remain unvalidated and should not be treated as causal or generalizable.\n\nIteration 15 outcome: The secondary leads were mostly not supported. H192 and H195 leave feature_011 outcome_014 as a positive but imprecise and non-localized lead; H196 rejects the feature_060=1 interaction within feature_002=1. Companion tests reject feature_011 transfer to outcome_011 (H194) and feature_006 transfer to outcome_006 in the localized cell (H193). The feature_007 reversed weaker-dependency lead is closed: H191 is opposite/imprecise, H198/H199 interactions are not supportive, and stratified mean differences are wide or null; H165 remains unresolved but closed because its statistically positive global outcome_006 estimate has lower bound below practical threshold. The feature_063 reversed lead is downgraded: H190 outcome_006 companion is inconclusive and H197 outcome_011 is null; H189 remains unresolved/deferred only for historical completeness. Broad screens H31 and H33 are null/opposite and closed.\n\nNext strategic guidance: Avoid reopening feature_007, feature_063, and the feature_011 outcome_014/outcome_011 companions unless there is a new validation opportunity. If any future analysis is needed, it should be extremely focused and not expand the accepted set. No independent validation remains, so conclusions remain associative and context-specific."
