y meaningful claim; it also implies the accepted older-stratum signal H223 should not be interpreted as a robust global older effect.\n\nH238 (R233) tested a global feature_006 age interaction. The signed estimate is +0.0395, interval -0.0818 to +0.1608. It neither excludes the null nor clears the practical threshold. There is no evidence for clinically meaningful global age modification of the feature_006/outcome_014 lead; reject and close.\n\nH239 (R234) tested feature_020 versus outcome_006 in the older feature_061>=54 stratum within feature_002=1. The signed estimate is +0.0990, interval +0.0026 to +0.1953, exposed n=77. The point estimate is in the expected weaker-dependency direction and nominally excludes the null, but the lower bound is below the practical threshold for outcome_006. Thus the evidence supports a statistically suggestive smaller effect but not a clinically meaningful older-stratum localization of H114; reject and close.\n\nH240 (R235) tested the corresponding younger feature_061<=53 stratum within feature_002=1. The signed estimate is +0.0486, interval -0.0557 to +0.1529. It crosses the null and fails the practical lower-bound rule; reject and close.\n\nH241 (R236) tested whether the feature_020/outcome_006 association within feature_002=1 differs between feature_060=1 and feature_060=0. The signed interaction is +0.0216, interval -0.1064 to +0.1496. It is small, imprecise, and below the practical threshold. This does not localize H114 to feature_060=1; reject and close. H213 remains unresolved but closed as a suggestive localization rather than an accepted localization.\n\nH242 (R237) tested feature_011 versus outcome_006 in the rare feature_002=1/feature_060=1 cell after excluding feature_020=1, to probe whether the accepted H179 association is independent of the feature_020 overlap. The signed estimate is +0.0558, interval -0.0330 to +0.1446, exposed n=67. It crosses the null and fails the practical threshold, so the rare-cell feature_011 lead is not robust to removing feature_020=1. This raises the competing explanation that H179 may partly reflect feature_020 structure or chance subgroup selection; reject and close.\n\nOverall, none of the new comparisons adds an accepted localization or robustness support to the accepted dataset-specific leads. The feature_006/outcome_014 lead remains accepted globally and within feature_060=0, with older-stratum evidence only inside feature_060=0, but not as a global older effect or as demonstrated age modification. The feature_020/outcome_006 lead remains accepted only as the aggregate feature_002=1 effect, without clinically robust age or feature_060 localization. The feature_011/outcome_006 rare-cell lead is weakened by the H242 robustness failure and should be regarded as the least reliable accepted lead. Multiple comparisons, small exposed cells, post-hoc subgroup refinement, and lack of external validation preclude causal or generalizable interpretation.",
 "research_notes": "Final appraise update after iteration 19/25. Validation budget is exhausted; no validation request is possible. Interpret all estimates as signed to the hypothesis direction and accept only when the signed lower confidence bound clears the outcome-specific practical 10%-relative threshold. Practical thresholds: outcome_014/outcome_006 about 0.0093; outcome_012 about 0.025; outcome_008 about 0.028; outcome_001 about 0.042.\n\nNew due comparisons H235-H242 are closed without acceptance. They do not support clinically meaningful localization of the accepted leads. H235-H238: feature_006/outcome_014 older signal within feature_060=0 does not replicate as a clinically robust older-global effect and is not supported as an age interaction. H239-H241: feature_020/outcome_006 within feature_002=1 is not clinically robustly localized to older age, younger age, or feature_060=1 relative to feature_060=0. H242: the rare-cell feature_011/outcome_006 lead fails when excluding feature_020=1, so its independence from feature_020 structure is not supported; this should sharply reduce confidence in H179.\n\nAccepted dataset-specific associative leads remain unchanged: feature_006=1 associated with stronger outcome_014 globally and most defensibly within feature_060=0, with an older feature_061>=54 localization inside feature_060=0 and a narrow feature_002=1/feature_060=0 cell localization; feature_020=1 associated with weaker outcome_006 within feature_002=1; feature_011=1 associated with stronger outcome_006 only in the rare feature_002=1/feature_060=1 cell, but this is the weakest lead because the H242 feature_020-exclusion test did not support independence.\n\nNo causal or generalizable claims are warranted. The predictors are opaque, analyses are observational, and many subgroup findings have small exposed cells and wide intervals. If external validation ever becomes available, prioritize feature_006/outcome_014 globally and within feature_060=0, then the older feature_060=0 localization and feature_002=1/feature_060=0 cell localization; secondarily validate feature_020/outcome_006 within feature_002=1. Deprioritize feature_011 unless targeted enrichment of feature_002=1/feature_060=1 and feature_020-exclusion testing are possible. Further internal discovery is low yield and high multiplicity risk; any future internal work should be restricted to preplanned robustness tests with the same lower-bound practical rule and closed investigation status."
