  "narrative": "No new validation was delivered and no claim response deadlines were pending. The voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so no new validation request was made. I close H155 and H206 as accepted within this supplied dataset only; this closure is final for this run and should not be read as independent validation, causal evidence, or generalizability.\n\nFinal decision rule used throughout: all returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1, a positive signed estimate means exposed-minus-comparator is more negative, i.e. stronger CRISPR dependency; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means exposed-minus-comparator is less negative, i.e. weaker dependency. Discovery claims were accepted as practically meaningful only when the signed lower 95% Welch confidence bound cleared the outcome-specific 10% practical threshold. For outcome_014 and outcome_006, because their mean absolute dependency scale is approximately 0.09, this threshold is about 0.0093 on the absolute dependency-score scale. Statistical significance alone was not treated as sufficient.\n\nSupported dataset-specific associative findings:\n1. Strongest robust lead: feature_020=1 is associated with weaker outcome_006 dependency within feature_002=1. Discovery H114/R83: +0.0853, 95% +0.0215 to +0.1492. Independence robustness H245/R240, after excluding feature_011=1, remained clinically meaningful: +0.1048, 95% +0.0359 to +0.1737. This is the most defensible accepted association because it retained the practical lower-bound rule after removing a nearby correlated predictor candidate. It remains associative, dataset-specific, and non-causal.\n2. feature_006=1 is associated with stronger outcome_014 dependency globally. H155/R141: +0.0647, 95% +0.0108 to +0.1186. The better localized version is within feature_060=0, H206/R200: +0.0881, 95% +0.0178 to +0.1584. These are accepted in the supplied dataset but with an explicit caveat: feature_020-exclusion robustness checks did not clear the practical rule. H243/R238 within feature_060=0 and feature_020=0 gave +0.0747, 95% -0.0060 to +0.1554; H244/R239 globally within feature_020=0 gave +0.0519, 95% -0.0084 to +0.1122. Therefore H155/H206 should be interpreted as contextual marker associations, not established independent predictor effects.\n3. Narrow feature_006/outcome_014 localizations that cleared the practical rule: H223/R218 within feature_060=0 and feature_061>=54 gave +0.1495, 95% +0.0453 to +0.2536; H168/R160 within feature_002=1 and feature_060=0 gave +0.1128, 95% +0.0175 to +0.2081. These support narrow dataset-specific localizations. They do not prove age modification, feature_002 modification, or a general subgroup structure.\n\nKey negative findings and disconfirming patterns:\n- Independent validation did not confirm any previously discovered lead at a clinically meaningful level. Failures include H8/R13, H15/R26, H24/R40, H34/R65, H37/R132, H39/R39, H54/R78, H63/R79, H88/R106, H94/R92 and its direction counterpart H96/R92, H110/R105, H139/R119, and H149/R145. This pattern strongly counsels against overgeneralizing subgroup discoveries in this dataset.\n- The feature_006 lead did not transfer to other tested outcomes in the feature_060=0 context: outcome_006 H224/R219, outcome_008 H225/R220, and outcome_001 H226/R221 failed practical relevance. It also did not clear practical relevance in feature_060=1 H210/R206 or in the feature_002=0 complement H211/R207.\n- The feature_020/outcome_006 lead did not transfer to outcome_014 H227/R222, outcome_001 H228/R223, or outcome_008 H229/R224 within feature_002=1. Its age and feature_060 localizations were not clinically established: H239/R234, H240/R235, and H241/R236 failed the lower-bound rule, and H213/R209 had a lower bound below the practical threshold.\n- Age and interaction tests for feature_006/outcome_014 did not establish effect modification. The global older-stratum estimate H237/R232 was +0.0819 but had lower bound +0.0014, and the corresponding interactions H236/R231 and H238/R233 failed. The younger feature_061<=53 test within feature_060=0 H235/R230 also failed.\n- The feature_011/outcome_006 rare-cell lead is not included as a supported finding. H179/R172 had discovery +0.0926, 95% +0.0114 to +0.1739, but it is unresolved because independence probes failed: H242/R237 feature_020-exclusion gave +0.0558, 95% -0.0330 to +0.1446, and H246/R241 feature_006-exclusion gave +0.0814, 95% -0.0037 to +0.1664. It should be deprioritized unless a targeted design can directly test independence from feature_006 and feature_020 and adequately enrich the relevant cells.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty: biological mechanism cannot be inferred from opaque predictor names; the design is observational; and extensive subgroup exploration creates winner-curse risk. Feature_006/outcome_014 remains a dataset-specific marker association whose independence from feature_020 structure is not established. Feature_020/outcome_006 within feature_002=1 is accepted, but whether feature_060, age, or other modifiers genuinely change the effect remains unresolved. Outcome specificity and the exact minimal sufficient subgroup definitions remain uncertain.\n\nMost informative next analysis: if external validation becomes available, the highest-priority preplanned test is feature_020 versus outcome_006 within feature_002=1, pre-specified as H114 with a planned robustness/adjustment check after excluding or adjusting feature_011 and feature_006, because H245/R240 already demonstrated practical robustness in the discovery data. A secondary preplanned test is feature_006 versus outcome_014 within feature_060=0, prioritizing H206 and global H155 but with explicit feature_020 independence checks; without such checks, replication may be confounded by feature_020 structure. H179 should not be prioritized unless rare-cell enrichment and independence testing are possible. Within the supplied dataset, further broad discovery is unlikely to add decision-relevant value under the current evidence rule and would increase multiplicity; only preplanned precision or robustness checks would be justified.",
  "research_notes": "Final run notes. No new validation, no response deadlines, validation budget exhausted. Accepted and closed current leads: strongest is feature_020=1 associated with weaker outcome_006 dependency within feature_002=1 (H114/R83), robust to feature_011 exclusion (H245/R240). feature_006=1 associated with stronger outcome_014 dependency globally (H155/R141) and localized in feature_060=0 (H206/R200), but feature_020-exclusion checks failed practical lower-bound rule (H243/R238, H244/R239), so these are conditional marker associations, not independent predictor claims. Narrow accepted feature_006/outcome_014 localizations H223/R218 and H168/R160 do not establish interaction. feature_011/outcome_006 rare-cell lead H179 remains unresolved and deprioritized because independence probes H242/R237 and H246/R241 failed. All independent validation attempts failed. No causal, mechanistic, or generalizable conclusions are supported. If external validation is possible, prioritize feature_020/outcome_006 within feature_002=1 first; secondary feature_006/outcome_014 within feature_060=0 with preplanned feature_020 independence checks. No further broad internal discovery is warranted."
