  "narrative": "All newly delivered estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For outcome_006 and outcome_014, the 10% practical threshold on the absolute mean-dependency scale is about 0.0093; for the other outcomes with absolute means near 0.25, it is about 0.0245 to 0.0415. I accepted no new clinically meaningful positive association because none had a signed 95% Welch lower bound clearing the outcome-specific threshold. H269/R264 is the feature_002-complement probe of the primary feature_020/outcome_006 lead: signed effect +0.0762 with interval -0.0326 to +0.1850 and exposed/comparator cells 59/380. It is directionally positive but underpowered and incompatible with either confirming a clinically meaningful feature_002=0 association or ruling one out; the feature_002-specific character of the accepted lead remains dataset-supported but not generalized. H270/R265 is the feature_006/outcome_014 independence probe after excluding feature_020=1 and feature_011=1 within feature_060=0: +0.0655, interval -0.0265 to +0.1575, cells 55/658. It leaves feature_006 independence from feature_020 unresolved rather than establishing independence. The outcome-specificity tests H271-H280 within feature_002=1, feature_060=0, feature_011=0 show no new robust cross-outcome effect. H273/R268 outcome_007 and H277/R272 outcome_012 have signed point estimates opposite the hypothesized weaker-dependency direction and upper bounds below the practical threshold, so clinically meaningful positive associations are rejected for those outcomes. H278/R273 outcome_013 is the only positive significant signal, +0.0734 with lower +0.0214, but the lower bound is below the 10% threshold of about 0.0269; given the high multiplicity and small exposed cell, it should not be promoted as meaningful. The remaining outcome tests are inconclusive because their intervals include clinically meaningful positive effects while lower bounds do not clear the threshold. Critically, exposed cells are small, intervals are wide, and this iteration occurs after repeated subgroup discovery and multiple failed validations; the appropriate inference is that no new clinically meaningful predictor or subgroup association is established. Existing accepted leads remain in-dataset associative only, outcome-specific, noncausal, and not independently validated or generalizable. No validation was requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 24 appraisal. No validation request is possible or made; remaining_new_requests=0. New evidence assessed: H269-H280. Practical rule unchanged: accept a positive association only when the signed lower 95% Welch bound exceeds the 10% absolute-mean threshold, about 0.0093 for outcome_006/outcome_014 and about 0.0245-0.0415 for other outcomes depending on their mean absolute dependency score. H269/R264: feature_020 vs 0 on outcome_006 in feature_002=0, feature_060=0, feature_011=0 gave +0.0762 [-0.0326,0.1850], n=59/380; unresolved/closed. It neither refutes nor supports feature_002-specificity. H270/R265: feature_006 vs 0 on outcome_014 in feature_060=0, feature_020=0, feature_011=0 gave +0.0655 [-0.0265,0.1575], n=55/658; unresolved/closed; independence from feature_020 not established. H271-H280 tested feature_020 across other outcomes in robust feature_002=1, feature_060=0, feature_011=0 population. No accepts. H273/R268 outcome_007 -0.0191 [-0.0615,0.0233] and H277/R272 outcome_012 -0.0245 [-0.0729,0.0239] reject clinically meaningful positive effects because upper bounds are below threshold. H278/R273 outcome_013 +0.0734 [0.0214,0.1255] is statistically positive but below practical threshold and underpowered/multiplicity-fragile, so unresolved/closed, not accepted. Other H271-H276 and H279-H280 have intervals compatible with clinically meaningful positive effects but lower bounds do not clear threshold; marked unresolved/closed because no further validation budget and further same-dataset mining has high false-discovery risk. Overall conclusion: the previously accepted dataset-specific leads remain: feature_020=1 associated with weaker outcome_006 dependency within feature_002=1 (especially after excluding feature_006=1 and/or feature_011=1); feature_006=1 associated with stronger outcome_014 dependency as an association, not proven independent of feature_020. No established modifiers, no causal mechanism, no biological interpretation, and no transportability. The most important remaining scientific uncertainty is external pre-specified validation with adequate cells for feature_020/outcome_006 within feature_002=1 and feature_006/outcome_014 within feature_060=0, with pre-specified interactions for feature_002, age, feature_050, feature_034, feature_060, feature_011, and feature_006 as appropriate."
